invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_mont.c
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test
reason: rsa_mont.c's kernel_takes admits an even modulus, so rsa_vp1_cpu
  hands rsa_ifma_public a modulus that has no inverse of its low digit,
  and the kernel writes other bytes than rsa_vp1, whose answer rsa.h
  promises for every input under the bit, an even n included.
  bin/rsa_ifma_model_test compares rsa_vp1_cpu under the bit with rsa_vp1
  for an even modulus that the dispatch must refuse.

--- old
    return k >= words_min && bit_length(n, n_len) == 64 * k && (n[n_len - 1] & 1) == 1;
--- new
    return k >= words_min && bit_length(n, n_len) == 64 * k;
